<body>
<div class="page">
<header class="title-block"><p class="eyebrow">Lumopolis documentation</p><h1>How Termpolis works</h1><p>Generated by Termpolis Lumopolis from the code</p><p>Project: Termpolis</p><p>Generated on 2026-11-21</p><p>Commit a1b2c3d, with changes not yet committed</p></header>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents"><p class="toc-title">Contents</p><ol><li><a href="#coverage">Coverage</a></li><li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li><li><a href="#glance">The city at a glance</a></li><li><a href="#runs">How it runs</a></li><li><a href="#areas">Areas</a><ol><li><a href="#s1">Core</a></li><li><a href="#s19">Agents</a></li></ol></li><li><a href="#connections">Connections</a></li><li><a href="#flows">Main flows</a></li><li><a href="#outside">Outside systems</a></li><li><a href="#planned">Planned changes</a></li><li><a href="#glossary">Glossary</a></li><li><a href="#notCovered">What this document doesn&#39;t cover yet</a></li></ol></nav>
<main><section class="chapter" id="coverage"><h2>Coverage</h2><p>3 of 3 parts and 3 of 4 connections are described.</p><p>Statements marked <em>inferred</em> come from reading the code, <em>verified</em> from tests or a person, <em>observed</em> from the code itself.</p></section>
<section class="chapter" id="overview"><h2>Overview</h2><p>Termpolis has 2 areas, 3 parts and 4 connections.</p><p>It runs as 3 processes: Main process, Memory host, Spare worker.</p><p>It is built with electron, ipc, sqlite.</p><ul><li>Core: The app and its memory</li><li>Agents: Where the agents run</li></ul></section>
<section class="chapter" id="glance"><h2>The city at a glance</h2><figure class="map"><svg class="lm-map" viewBox="-12 -12 816 129.1" width="816" height="129.1" role="img" aria-label="Map of 2 areas and the connections between them" style="width: 51rem; min-width: 816px"><defs><marker id="lm-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="11" markerHeight="11" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto"><path class="lm-arrowhead" d="M0 1L10 5L0 9z"/></marker></defs><path class="lm-line" d="M338 87.8 Q396 101.7 449 89" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#lm-arrow)"/><g data-id="d1" class="lm-area"><title>Core: The app and its memory</title><rect class="lm-box" x="0" y="0" width="336" height="94" rx="12"/><text class="lm-area-name" x="14" y="24">Core</text><text class="lm-area-meta" x="14" y="41">2 parts · 2 connections inside</text><rect class="lm-part" x="14" y="52" width="150" height="28" rx="6"><title>Desktop app</title></rect><text class="lm-part-label" x="24" y="66" dominant-baseline="central">Desktop app</text><rect class="lm-part" x="172" y="52" width="150" height="28" rx="6"><title>Memory host</title></rect><text class="lm-part-label" x="182" y="66" dominant-baseline="central">Memory host</text></g><g data-id="d2" class="lm-area"><title>Agents: Where the agents run</title><rect class="lm-box" x="456" y="0" width="336" height="94" rx="12"/><text class="lm-area-name" x="470" y="24">Agents</text><text class="lm-area-meta" x="470" y="41">1 part</text><rect class="lm-part" x="470" y="52" width="150" height="28" rx="6"><title>Agent runner</title></rect><text class="lm-part-label" x="480" y="66" dominant-baseline="central">Agent runner</text></g><g class="lm-count"><title>1 connection from Core to Agents</title><rect x="384" y="85.1" width="21.5" height="20" rx="10"/><text x="394.8" y="95.1" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">1</text></g></svg><figcaption>Each box is an area with its parts inside. An arrow between two areas counts the connections running that way.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="chapter" id="runs"><h2>How it runs</h2><p>Each process and the parts that run in it.</p><ul><li>Main process: Desktop app, Agent runner</li><li>Memory host: Memory host</li><li>Spare worker</li></ul></section>
<section class="chapter" id="areas"><h2>Areas</h2><section class="area" id="s1"><h3>Core</h3><p>The app and its memory</p><section class="part" id="s2"><h4>Desktop app</h4><p>Electron + React</p><p>Status: Built · not yet checked</p><p>Runs in: Main process</p><section class="field" id="s3"><h5>What it does</h5><ul class="claims"><li><span class="badge badge-observed">observed</span> <span class="claim">The main process opens the window and hosts terminals.</span><span class="refs"><code>file src/main/index.ts</code></span></li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s4"><h5>What&#39;s inside</h5><ul><li>Window shell · electron: src/main/shell/part0.ts, src/main/shell/part1.ts, src/main/shell/part2.ts, src/main/shell/part3.ts, src/main/shell/part4.ts, src/main/shell/part5.ts, src/main/shell/part6.ts, src/main/shell/part7.ts, src/main/shell/part8.ts, src/main/shell/part9.ts, src/main/shell/part10.ts, src/main/shell/part11.ts and 3 more</li><li>Menus</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s5"><h5>Why it is this big</h5><p>15 files. It started as the entry of the &quot;main&quot; process. 2 name families and 1 single file were merged in because of dense imports. 3 files imported only from inside it joined it. 1 other group was folded in because Lumopolis shows at most 30 buildings per project. Its floors are listed under What&#39;s inside.</p></section><section class="field" id="s6"><h5>Technology</h5><ul><li>electron: A framework for desktop apps.</li><li>ipc: How two programs talk.</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s7"><h5>Why it&#39;s built this way</h5><ul class="claims"><li><span class="badge badge-inferred">inferred</span> <span class="claim">One shell hosts every agent terminal.</span><span class="refs"><code>file docs/architecture.md</code></span></li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s8"><h5>What we know</h5><ul class="claims"><li><span class="badge badge-verified">verified</span> <span class="claim">Startup is covered by a test.</span><span class="refs"><code>test tests/main/startup.test.ts (report)</code></span></li><li><span class="badge badge-verified">verified</span> <span class="claim">The window opens maximised.</span><span class="refs"><code>person David</code></span></li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s9"><h5>What comes in</h5><ul><li>Memory replies from Memory host: Both ways: Memory host reaches Desktop app, and Desktop app reaches Memory host.</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s10"><h5>What goes out</h5><ul><li>Memory calls to Memory host: Both ways: Desktop app reaches Memory host, and Memory host reaches Desktop app.</li><li>reads 1 setting +1 more to Agent runner: One way: Desktop app reaches Agent runner; the code shows no line from Agent runner back to Desktop app.</li></ul></section></section><section class="part" id="s11"><h4>Memory host</h4><p>Node + SQLite</p><p>Status: Built · tests pass</p><p>Runs in: Memory host</p><section class="field" id="s12"><h5>What it does</h5><ul class="claims"><li><span class="badge badge-verified">verified</span> <span class="claim">Memories are stored in a local SQLite database.</span><span class="refs"><code>file src/main/memory/store.ts</code></span></li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s13"><h5>What&#39;s inside</h5><ul><li>Floor 1 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f0.ts</li><li>Floor 2 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f1.ts</li><li>Floor 3 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f2.ts</li><li>Floor 4 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f3.ts</li><li>Floor 5 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f4.ts</li><li>Floor 6 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f5.ts</li><li>Floor 7 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f6.ts</li><li>Floor 8 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f7.ts</li><li>Floor 9 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f8.ts</li><li>Floor 10 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f9.ts</li><li>Floor 11 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f10.ts</li><li>Floor 12 · sqlite: src/main/memory/f11.ts</li><li>and 1 more</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s14"><h5>Technology</h5><ul><li>sqlite: A small database in one file.</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s15"><h5>Why it&#39;s built this way</h5><ul class="claims"><li><span class="badge badge-inferred">inferred</span> <span class="claim">Agents share what they learn without a cloud service.</span><span class="refs"><code>file src/a.ts</code></span></li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s16"><h5>Service names</h5><p>memory-host, brain (edited by you)</p></section><section class="field" id="s17"><h5>What comes in</h5><ul><li>Memory calls from Desktop app: Both ways: Desktop app reaches Memory host, and Memory host reaches Desktop app.</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s18"><h5>What goes out</h5><ul><li>Memory replies to Desktop app: Both ways: Memory host reaches Desktop app, and Desktop app reaches Memory host.</li></ul></section></section></section><section class="area" id="s19"><h3>Agents</h3><p>Where the agents run</p><section class="part" id="s20"><h4>Agent runner (name suggested by AI)</h4><p>Status: Built · no test results yet</p><p>Runs in: Main process</p><section class="field" id="s21"><h5>What it does</h5><ul class="claims"><li><span class="badge badge-inferred">inferred</span> <span class="claim">Starts each agent in its own terminal.</span><span class="refs"><code>file src/a.ts</code></span></li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s22"><h5>Why it&#39;s built this way</h5><p>Not described yet.</p></section><section class="field" id="s23"><h5>What comes in</h5><ul><li>reads 1 setting +1 more from Desktop app: One way: Desktop app reaches Agent runner; the code shows no line from Agent runner back to Desktop app.</li></ul></section><section class="field" id="s24"><h5>What goes out</h5><ul><li>calls 1 web address to Model API: One way, with replies: Agent runner asks and Model API answers.</li></ul></section></section></section></section>
<section class="chapter" id="connections"><h2>Connections</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>What travels</th><th>How</th><th>Direction</th><th>Why</th><th>How often</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Desktop app</td><td>Memory host</td><td>Memory: Memory calls</td><td>The app calls the memory host over a local socket. [observed]; Technology: ipc; What we know: Each call is answered within a second. [verified]</td><td>Both ways: Desktop app reaches Memory host, and Memory host reaches Desktop app.</td><td>Keeps the database out of the UI process. [inferred]</td><td>on demand</td></tr><tr><td>Memory host</td><td>Desktop app</td><td>Memory: Memory replies</td><td>The host answers each call. [inferred]</td><td>Both ways: Memory host reaches Desktop app, and Desktop app reaches Memory host.</td><td>Not described yet; the code alone does not say why.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Desktop app</td><td>Agent runner</td><td>env AGENT_HOME, ipc agent:start</td><td>From the code: Desktop app reaches Agent runner this way: it reads 1 setting and uses 1 message channel.</td><td>One way: Desktop app reaches Agent runner; the code shows no line from Agent runner back to Desktop app.</td><td>Not described yet; the code alone does not say why.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Agent runner</td><td>Model API</td><td>http-out api.example.com</td><td>The runner calls the service. [inferred]</td><td>One way, with replies: Agent runner asks and Model API answers.</td><td>Not described yet; the code alone does not say why.</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="chapter" id="flows"><h2>Main flows</h2><section class="sub" id="s25"><h3>First look</h3><ol class="steps"><li>The app talks to its memory. (Core, Desktop app → Memory host, Memory host)</li><li>That is all.</li></ol></section></section>
<section class="chapter" id="outside"><h2>Outside systems</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>What it is</th><th>Reached by</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Model API (not seen in code)</td><td>provider</td><td>Agent runner</td></tr><tr><td>Shared drive</td><td>files</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="chapter" id="planned"><h2>Planned changes</h2><p>No planned changes are recorded.</p></section>
<section class="chapter" id="glossary"><h2>Glossary</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>electron</td><td>A framework for desktop apps.</td></tr><tr><td>ipc</td><td>How two programs talk.</td></tr><tr><td>sqlite</td><td>A small database in one file.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="chapter" id="notCovered"><h2>What this document doesn&#39;t cover yet</h2><p>These connections are not described yet:</p><ul><li>reads 1 setting +1 more (Desktop app → Agent runner)</li></ul><p>Lumopolis reads the code, not the running app: it does not see runtime behaviour or data contents.</p></section></main>
<footer class="colophon"><p>Made with Lumopolis in Termpolis · <a href="https://termpolis.com">termpolis.com</a></p></footer>
</div>
